  "storyId": "B-7036",
  "name": "ablation-analysis",
  "title": "Add the section5/6 powered-ablation analysis script: common-cell denominators + per-arm rates + A4-vs-A2prime cluster-bootstrap contrast + FDR + GLMM emission",
  "description": "infra-(a) piece 5 (final infra piece) of the powered-ablation program. The run driver (B-f248) emits section-7 run-records JSONL; what is missing is the deterministic, offline analysis layer that turns those records into the pre-registered readouts. It reads the section-7 JSONL, applies the section-7 validity filter (void becomes excluded as re-run, task-failures kept, N/A excluded), computes the section-5 common-cell denominators for each of the 4 pre-registered contrasts (rates ONLY over cells applicable to BOTH arms), per-arm outcome rates (section-4.1 completion for the null-ablation cells; section-4.2 not-amplified/recovered/safe-stop for the recovery scenarios) with Wilson 95 percent CIs, the PRIMARY A4-vs-A2prime contrast via a seeded cluster bootstrap (resampling task/scenario clusters into a risk-difference plus 95 percent CI accounting for within-cell dependence; the in-Node verifiable proxy for the GLMM), Benjamini-Hochberg FDR over the exploratory per-scenario tests, and the cost co-metric (tokens plus wall-clock per arm). It emits a tidy long-format CSV (one row per run with all factors) plus a glmm.R (lme4 glmer arm fixed plus random task/scenario/seed) for the formal pre-registered GLMM. Everything is deterministic and offline-testable with synthetic fixtures (no live LLM).",
